From d0879328829eccf55f7c78ce2356190aefe2ae96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:24:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional stereo 3D view

With --stereo the view asks for left and right buffers
(QSurfaceFormat::StereoBuffers). QOpenGLWidget then calls paintGL()
once per eye, and the cubes are drawn by two cameras either side of the
usual one: parallel, meeting at the distance of the cubes' centres, so
the cubes' centre has no parallax and parts nearer or further shift
in opposite directions. The scene is built once, only the projection
differs; the modelview matrix, the background picture and the labels
are the same in both eyes. The mouse picking uses the left eye.
--stereo-separation sets the distance between the eyes, in percent of
the distance to the cubes.

Without --stereo, or when the platform gives no stereo buffers, the
view is drawn as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
